  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Cure TB Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kyrgyz Republic):  Cure Tuberculosis (TB) reduces the burden of drug-resistant TB (DR-TB) in the Kyrgyz Republic. To achieve this, the activity will increase DR-TB case detection in primary health care and community-based settings; improve laboratory services and networks; increase the treatment success rate by ensuring that patients are treated with the appropriate drug regimens and by providing case management support for patients to complete their treatment; prevent DR-TB infections through improved infection control in health facilities and laboratories; change provider, patient, and at-risk populations behaviors for improved TB prevention, detection, and treatment; and improve the enabling environment for sustainable TB services through improved financing for TB services, improved data for decision making, updated policies, and reduced stigma and discrimination.  The activity will achieve these goals through a combination of technical assistance, mentoring, policy formation, and advocacy. The combination of these efforts will build on the previous programming and address constraints in reducing the transmission of DR-TB within the Kyrgyz Republic...This activity also supports ICS objective 3.2: Government institutions that can effectively formulate and implement policies and provide quality services in an equitable, transparent, and accountable way..This IM  contributes $4,070,000 toward the  $6,000,000 FY 2022 Operating Unit TB directive. .. .</narrative>
  </description>
